(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "honest record of an OPEN, UNRESOLVED defect in kotoba.sm.gtg's Phase 1\n    field-equation pipeline (omega-from-h/riemann-map/riemann-basis-pair/\n    curvature-scalar) -- not a fix. Documented prominently in code (PR #14,\n    docstring-only, no behavior change) rather than left as a latent trap" "BUG: curvature-scalar returns EXACTLY 7x the correct value for any h-field\n    with genuinely time-varying expansion rate (Hdot!=0) -- e.g. Einstein-de\n    Sitter matter-dominated dust, H(t)=2/(3t). Independently reproduced by 2\n    people (investigating agent + requester in a fresh REPL), ratio stable at\n    7.00000000 (7-8 sig figs) across fd-h in [5e-5,1e-3] and t in [1.5,10] --\n    a clean algebraic sign error, not FD truncation noise" "correct answer independently confirmed GTG-FREE: ordinary Christoffel-symbol\n    computation on the metric this h-bar represents gives R=-12*H^2-6*Hdot\n    (standard FRW textbook result); this pipeline computes -12*H^2+6*Hdot --\n    ONLY the Hdot (time-derivative) term has wrong sign, H^2 term is exactly\n    correct" "why undetected by 2 prior independent reviews: BOTH existing regression\n    solutions (Schwarzschild=static, de Sitter=constant H) have Hdot=0\n    identically, structurally cannot exercise the time-derivative channel.\n    FOURTH instance of silently-wrong-result-surviving-review in this repo's\n    GTG work (after PR #6 slot order, Phase 1 first-attempt wrong covariant\n    derivative, PR #11 double-h bug) -- first that 2 independent multi-hour\n    investigations could NOT resolve to a confident root cause" "what was checked and found individually correct in isolation: H-field\n    (symbolic general H(t), structurally zero Hdot-dependence by construction),\n    omega-from-h (checked against eq 4.50 directly + independent Python GA\n    engine, exact match), L-a-omega (eq 4.42 identity a.hbar(grad)F=h(a).grad F\n    verified on a PLAIN SCALAR test function F(x)=t,a=e_0, no bivector/GA\n    machinery -- exact match; commutator eq 4.44 also checked directly,\n    matched to 1e-13), riemann-basis-pair (eq 4.44->4.46->4.47->4.48 chain\n    re-derived by hand, line-by-line match). YET end-to-end composition is\n    measurably wrong specifically in the time-derivative channel. Symbolic\n    isolation: code computes R(e0^e1)=-H^2+H', correct tetrad value is\n    -H^2-H'" "declined patch: negating L-a-omega's rho=0 (time-direction) contribution\n    only numerically fixes the dust case and provably doesn't affect\n    Schwarzschild/de-Sitter (both structurally zero rho=0 contribution) --\n    but DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED because it contradicts the simpler,\n    independent scalar-function identity check (a.hbar(grad)F=h(a).grad F on\n    F(x)=t) -- applying the patch would make THAT more fundamental check\n    fail. Symptom suppression, not a verified fix; would reintroduce exactly\n    the tests-pass-code-is-wrong failure mode this investigative lineage\n    exists to prevent" "decision: do not land any fix without confident independently-verified\n    root cause. Document prominently instead (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED BUG notice\n    in namespace docstring PHASE 1 SCOPE NOTE + curvature-scalar's own\n    docstring): Schwarzschild (static) and de Sitter (Hdot=0) remain verified\n    and safe; any h-field with Hdot!=0 is NOT safe to trust through this\n    pipeline until resolved. No new test added for dust case (would either\n    fail, or misleadingly signal resolved). No existing test/code modified --\n    79 tests/2911 assertions unchanged" "recommended next steps for future work: (1) GTG/geometric-algebra domain\n    expert consultation beyond what iterative independent re-derivation from\n    the primary paper alone achieved; (2) cross-check against a THIRD\n    independent exact time-dependent solution from literature (PDF page\n    images, not pdftotext); (3) consider whether bug is not in any single\n    named function but in an INTERACTION between H-field's INNER finite\n    difference (differentiating hbar^-1) and L-a-omega's OUTER finite\n    difference (differentiating omega-from-h itself) when both differentiate\n    along the SAME coordinate (t) -- a 'finite difference of a finite\n    difference' structure unique to this pipeline neither investigation\n    fully ruled out" "methodological consequence extending ADR-2607103000: fourth instance of\n    silently-wrong-invisible-to-tests failure mode, first that resisted 2\n    genuine independent resolution attempts. Response is NOT to force a fix,\n    guess-and-check against the one failing test, or lower the verification\n    bar -- document honestly, decline the unverified patch, leave the defect\n    visible. Future GTG regression solutions should be maximally DIFFERENT IN\n    KIND from what's covered (a genuinely time-VARYING rate, not just\n    'another named solution' -- de Sitter's own limitation despite being\n    literally time-dependent in its metric, Hdot=0 made it insufficient,\n    teaches this lesson)")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607103000" "adr-2607102700" "adr-2607102300")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607103600-kotoba-lang-standard-model-time-derivative-sign-bug-unresolved"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-09"), (:adr/body "see 2607103600-kotoba-lang-standard-model-time-derivative-sign-bug-unresolved.edn"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-09"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/addendum-2026-07-09 (vector "investigation 3 (nested-FD diagnostic, not a fix attempt): H-field's\n    inner finite difference replaced with an EXACT analytic closed-form\n    curl for the dust case -- bug persisted bit-for-bit identical. This\n    REFUTES the nested-finite-difference-interaction hypothesis and clears\n    H-field with proof (not just in-isolation verification): even a\n    zero-FD-error version does not change the outcome" "investigation 4 (term-by-term isolation, strongest method used yet): an\n    independent, from-scratch sympy reimplementation of eq (4.42)'s\n    directional derivative and eq (4.48)'s combination formula (built\n    directly from docstrings, no calls into the Clojure code) matched the\n    actual code term-by-term for ALL 6 basis-bivector pairs (not just one),\n    and hand-reconstructing curvature-scalar's full double sum from these\n    independently-verified values reproduces the wrong answer bit-for-bit.\n    This CLEARS L-a-omega and riemann-basis-pair as coding-level bugs (an\n    independently-authored, differently-implemented version of the same\n    documented math reproduces the identical wrong answer) -- a materially\n    stronger clearance than formula inspection alone. A speculative side-lead\n    (nonzero omega(e_0) correction) was tested and explicitly discarded --\n    broke the already-verified de Sitter case, not applied, not a finding" "after 4 independent investigations: H-field, L-a-omega, riemann-basis-pair\n    all cleared with strong non-code-reading evidence. Remaining candidates:\n    (a) omega-from-h's closed-form DERIVATION of eq (4.53) itself (distinct\n    from its eq-4.50 self-consistency, already verified), or (b) a conceptual\n    gap in applying eq (4.48) to genuinely time-evolving connections not\n    visible from formula re-derivation alone -- i.e. now a physics/derivation-\n    level question, not a code-level one. Status UNCHANGED: confirmed,\n    unresolved, documented (PR #14 docstring warnings remain accurate). Further\n    attempts should change METHOD (external GTG expertise, or a 5th\n    independent time-dependent solution from literature) rather than repeat\n    term-isolation at yet finer granularity -- already applied at 3\n    increasing levels (whole-function, all-terms-one-pair, all-terms-all-pairs)\n    without success")), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607103600: kotoba-lang/standard-model — a confirmed, currently-unresolved sign bug in Phase 1's field-equation pipeline for time-dependent position-gauge fields"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))